  "description": "OpenOmicsBench provides traceable offline benchmarks and processed-result assessments for RNA-seq, single-cell labels, DNA and protein sequences, genomic intervals and synthetic read-level taxonomy. Version 15 adds six sourced single-cell cases from one CellBench study, alongside the existing 16 bulk RNA-seq objects and synthetic fixtures. It adds reports for clusters and annotations, region-limited small variants, chromatin peaks and peptide identifications, plus optional AnnData export. The searchable catalog contains 31 objects. Source labels and declared references support bounded comparisons; they do not establish general biological ground truth.",
